From: ioswitch <noreply@ioswitch.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Blend extended-range attachments over unordered input attachments where neither ordered form exists

QuartzCore 21H461's MetalContext::warmup_shaders builds a fixed table of 560 pipeline specs, gated only by supportsFamily:.
With Apple3 answered true (the bridge's TARGET_FAMILIES, as on the real A10X), about 290 of the rows that fire render into
BGR10_XR ('w30r', 554) and RGB10A8_2P_XR10 ('b3a8', 550) with a blend (sov, add, din, dot, mul), whatever the display or
CADeviceUseCIF10 picks for real frames. The compile layer computes such a blend in the shader over the attachment's input
attachment only on a device with rasterization-order attachment access, or in the storage form inside the pixel interlock;
NVK on Maxwell (GM20B) has neither, so every one was refused Unsupported{Format, NotImplemented} at Color(0), and the first
refusal aborts backboardd (CA::OGL::MetalContext::create_pipeline_state, COREANIMATION code 4,
spec=Pw30rBsovXm_TaltA2Xhf_Isrc).

Under FramebufferFetchPolicy::AcceptUnordered on such a device the input-attachment blend now runs unordered, the trade
0001 already makes for every other fetch there (lower::fragment::blends_through_inputs, used by the input blend's plan, the
pass's fetch inputs, link's invariant and the format answer extended_range_blend): later draws blend over earlier draws'
codes (0001's barrier between fetching draws), fragments of one draw covering one pixel blend in no defined order, recorded
as PrecisionNote::UnorderedFramebufferFetch. Link also gives an extended-range attachment that no first output of the
function names no Vulkan blend (its raw format has none) and an empty mask: the draw leaves it unmodified, as Metal does,
instead of refusing the pipeline (the uber shader's specializations that write only the other attachment); not a bfloat
one (Metal refuses its blend) nor one of a pipeline without a fragment function, which stay refused as before. Test:
tests::engine_fragment::an_extended_range_blend_reads_unordered_input_attachments_where_neither_ordered_form_exists.
---
